      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/closed-card.ts",
      "content": "Short plans store signed negative quantities (for example, the cash-secured-put fixture uses `quantity: '-2'`). Using that value directly below renders “Sell -2 contracts”, and a one-contract short is incorrectly pluralized because `-1 !== 1`. Format the absolute planned quantity for both the unit selection and Entry text while retaining `side` to describe the direction; add a short-plan test using the actual signed representation.",
      "existing_code": "  const units = Number(plan.quantity) === 1 ? one : many;",
      "start_line": 42,
      "end_line": 42,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
